speechtext:
May I quote this description, which reads:
Materials used exclusively in the production of magazines and literary papers unbound, regularly issued at stated intervals, not less frequently than four times yearly;
Does this include church bulletins issued weekly which carry no advertising matter at all?

Yes; as a matter of fact it goes into the manufacture. It is used to produce the goods, definitely; and in this instance the goods, when produced, are taxable. So that, while it is not a component part, nevertheless it is used. Paragraph (f) says-
Materials which are consumed or expended In the manufacture or production of goods;
This conditioner definitely is consumed, along with the fuel oil. It is certainly expended.
